<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39192" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prōvectus</span></b> ,
			ūs, m.
		proveho (postclass.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Advancement</i>, <i>promotion</i> to
			places of honor: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">honestiorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aur.
					Vict. Caes. 39 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Progress</i>, <i>increase</i>, <i>furtherance</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aetatis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 4, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praesentia domini provectus est agri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pall. 1, 6, 1</span></i>
			.—<i>Plur.</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Amm. 28, 4, 20</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
